{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '150,260p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '410,485p'; rg -n 'quietly|links|assoc|update|merge|conj' src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc; tail -65 collab/1791275752148-repl-engineer-head-h3-r3.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\"","aggregated_output":"   150\t(defn render-heads\n   151\t  \"The text of `records`: one EDN map, with no whitespace before a\n   152\t   closing bracket (ClojureDart's reader refuses one).\"\n   153\t  [records]\n   154\t  (str (pr-str records) \"\\n\"))\n   155\t\n   156\t\n   157\t(defn- not-regular\n   158\t  []\n   159\t  (ex-info \"it is not a regular file\" {}))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- read-bounded\n   163\t  \"At most `limit` bytes of the file at `path`, one more when it holds\n   164\t   more, or nil when no entry exists there.  Never reads the whole of a\n   165\t   larger file into memory, and never opens what is not a regular file\n   166\t   (a directory, a FIFO, a device), which would block or fail: that is\n   167\t   refused first.  A symlink is followed when its target is a regular\n   168\t   file; a dangling one is refused.\"\n   169\t  [path limit]\n   170\t  #?(:cljd (let [t (.-type (.statSync (dart-io/File. path)))]\n   171\t             (cond\n   172\t               (= t dart-io/FileSystemEntityType.notFound)\n   173\t               ;; a dangling link is an entry, not absence\n   174\t               (when (.existsSync (dart-io/Link. path))\n   175\t                 (throw (not-regular)))\n   176\t\n   177\t               (not= t dart-io/FileSystemEntityType.file)\n   178\t               (throw (not-regular))\n   179\t\n   180\t               :else\n   181\t               (let [raf (.openSync (dart-io/File. path))]\n   182\t                 (try (.readSync raf (inc limit))\n   183\t                      (finally (.closeSync raf))))))\n   184\t     :clj (let [p (java.nio.file.Paths/get path (make-array String 0))]\n   185\t            (cond\n   186\t              (java.nio.file.Files/notExists\n   187\t                p (into-array java.nio.file.LinkOption\n   188\t                              [java.nio.file.LinkOption/NOFOLLOW_LINKS]))\n   189\t              nil\n   190\t\n   191\t              (not (java.nio.file.Files/isRegularFile\n   192\t                     p (make-array java.nio.file.LinkOption 0)))\n   193\t              (throw (not-regular))\n   194\t\n   195\t              :else\n   196\t              (with-open [in (java.nio.file.Files/newInputStream\n   197\t                               p (make-array java.nio.file.OpenOption 0))]\n   198\t                (.readNBytes in (int (inc limit))))))\n   199\t     :cljs (let [fs (js/require \"fs\")\n   200\t                 entry? (try (.lstatSync fs path) true\n   201\t                             (catch :default _ false))]\n   202\t             (when entry?\n   203\t               (when-not (try (.isFile (.statSync fs path))\n   204\t                              (catch :default _ false))\n   205\t                 (throw (not-regular)))\n   206\t               ;; non-blocking, then the opened resource is checked again\n   207\t               (let [fd (.openSync fs path (bit-or (.. fs -constants -O_RDONLY)\n   208\t                                                   (.. fs -constants -O_NONBLOCK)))\n   209\t                     buf (js/Buffer.alloc (inc limit))]\n   210\t                 (try\n   211\t                   (when-not (.isFile (.fstatSync fs fd))\n   212\t                     (throw (not-regular)))\n   213\t                   (loop [off 0]\n   214\t                     (let [n (.readSync fs fd buf off (- (inc limit) off) nil)\n   215\t                           off' (+ off n)]\n   216\t                       (if (and (pos? n) (< off' (inc limit)))\n   217\t                         (recur off')\n   218\t                         (.subarray buf 0 off'))))\n   219\t                   (finally (.closeSync fs fd))))))))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(defn- byte-length\n   223\t  [bs]\n   224\t  #?(:cljd (.-length ^Uint8List bs)\n   225\t     :clj (alength ^bytes bs)\n   226\t     :cljs (.-length bs)))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn- decode-utf8\n   230\t  \"`bs` as text, strictly: invalid UTF-8 throws, never decodes to a\n   231\t   replacement character.\"\n   232\t  [bs]\n   233\t  ;; Dart's `utf8` codec does not allow malformed input: it throws a\n   234\t  ;; FormatException\n   235\t  #?(:cljd (.decode convert/utf8 ^Uint8List bs)\n   236\t     :clj (str (.decode (doto (.newDecoder java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets/UTF_8)\n   237\t                          (.onMalformedInput\n   238\t                            java.nio.charset.CodingErrorAction/REPORT)\n   239\t                          (.onUnmappableCharacter\n   240\t                            java.nio.charset.CodingErrorAction/REPORT))\n   241\t                        (java.nio.ByteBuffer/wrap ^bytes bs)))\n   242\t     :cljs (.decode (js/TextDecoder. \"utf-8\" #js {:fatal true}) bs)))\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\t(defn read-heads\n   246\t  \"The persisted head records of the store directory `dir`: `{:records\n   247\t   r}`, an empty version-1 record when no `heads.edn` exists, or\n   248\t   `{:refusal text}`: a file that cannot be read, holds more than\n   249\t   `heads-max-bytes`, is not valid UTF-8, or is not exactly one\n   250\t   version-1 record.  Never throws.\"\n   251\t  [dir]\n   252\t  (let [path (str dir \"/\" heads-file)\n   253\t        bs (try (read-bounded path heads-max-bytes)\n   254\t                (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   255\t                  {::failed (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))\n   256\t        text (when (and (some? bs) (not (map? bs))\n   257\t                        (<= (byte-length bs) heads-max-bytes))\n   258\t               (try (decode-utf8 bs)\n   259\t                    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   260\t                      ::invalid)))]\n   410\t               (-> (dht/load-index manifest)\n   411\t                   (assoc ::hydrating manifest)))]\n   412\t    ;; a recovered HEAD's trace, so a reader's first contact needs no new\n   413\t    ;; round (5.4)\n   414\t    (when-some [recovered (and pub (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n   415\t      (deposit-head! pub recovered))\n   416\t    (assoc (dht/store node)\n   417\t           :head-fn (fn [manifest-address]\n   418\t                      ((:head-fn base) manifest-address)\n   419\t                      (dht/announce! node manifest-address)\n   420\t                      (when pub (deposit-head! pub manifest-address)))\n   421\t           :recovery (:recovery base)\n   422\t           :durable-dir dir\n   423\t           :dht node)))\n   424\t\n   425\t\n   426\t(defn- quietly!\n   427\t  \"Run the cleanup `f`, swallowing what it throws: a cleanup never\n   428\t   replaces the refusal that caused it.\"\n   429\t  [f]\n   430\t  (try (f) nil\n   431\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   432\t\n   433\t\n   434\t(defn open\n   435\t  \"Open a `dht:<dir>` store from its spec (yin.repl.store/checked-spec):\n   436\t   the durable directory store, and the `dao.space.dht` node joined over\n   437\t   it.  Answers the store handle the shell keeps (the node's store, with\n   438\t   the durable HEAD write announcing each publication, the recovery, and\n   439\t   the directory), carrying the node under `:dht`, which the shell moves\n   440\t   onto its own state (yin.repl/create-state).\n   441\t\n   442\t   `opts`: `:key`, the publisher key `{:seed :public}`, which makes a\n   443\t   publishing node deposit its head; `:ws`, the host WebSocket seam\n   444\t   `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (yin.repl.host) the board is served and\n   445\t   dialed over; `:write-heads!`, `(fn [dir name text])`, the atomic file\n   446\t   replace `heads.edn` is written with (`dao.space.store.fs` by\n   447\t   default); `:open-store`, `(fn [dir])`, the durable directory open\n   448\t   (`dao.space.store/open` by default).\n   449\t\n   450\t   A refusal releases everything it opened, exactly once, and is\n   451\t   answered as itself whatever the release throws: before the join the\n   452\t   directory store is closed; once joined the node owns it, and closing\n   453\t   the node closes the socket and then the store.\"\n   454\t  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n   455\t  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads! open-store]}]\n   456\t   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n   457\t                 manifest bind!]\n   458\t          :as checked} (store/checked-spec spec)\n   459\t         follow (checked-follow checked)\n   460\t         base ((or open-store durable/open) dir)\n   461\t         [node records]\n   462\t         (try\n   463\t           (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n   464\t                                         (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n   465\t             (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n   466\t           (let [records (heads-records dir follow)]\n   467\t             [(dht/join {:local base\n   468\t                         :peers peers\n   469\t                         :publish? publish?\n   470\t                         :bind-host bind-host\n   471\t                         :bind-port bind-port\n   472\t                         :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n   473\t                         :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n   474\t              records])\n   475\t           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   476\t             (quietly! #(store/close! base))\n   477\t             (throw e)))]\n   478\t     ;; from here the node owns the store and holds a socket\n   479\t     (try\n   480\t       (compose node base checked follow records\n   481\t                {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})\n   482\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   483\t         (quietly! #(dht/close! node))\n   484\t         (throw e))))))\n   485\t\n395:        node (cond-> (assoc node ::dir dir ::ws ws)\n396:               pub (assoc ::publisher pub)\n397:               follower (assoc ::follower follower\n405:                                :links {}\n411:                   (assoc ::hydrating manifest)))]\n416:    (assoc (dht/store node)\n426:(defn- quietly!\n476:             (quietly! #(store/close! base))\n483:         (quietly! #(dht/close! node))\n511:    (doseq [[_ {:keys [dial]}] (get-in node [::follow :links])]\n662:    [(assoc pub :server server :listen [host port])\n685:        pub (cond-> pub server (assoc :server server))\n689:                (conj (str \"dht: join token: \"\n693:                (conj (str \"dht: the head board could not bind TCP \"\n696:        pub (cond-> pub (= :serving (:status server)) (assoc :token? true))\n703:                                   :dao.stream/ok (recur (conj notes\n710:    [(assoc pub :notes-cursor cursor)\n712:         (cond-> lost? (conj (str \"dht: more head trace refusals arrived \"\n732:        (update :indexer index/rehydrate recovery)\n733:        (assoc :index-recovery recovery\n801:        [follower (assoc link :dial d :since now :handle nil) nil]))\n805:          link (assoc link :dial d)\n810:         (assoc link :handle h :delay nil :failed nil)\n823:(defn- step-links\n824:  \"Step every principal's dial: `[follower links lines]`, one line per\n827:  (let [{:keys [sources links]} (::follow node)]\n828:    (reduce (fn [[follower links lines] [p source]]\n833:                                                       ;; multi-key assoc on\n835:                                                       (get links p {})\n837:                    fresh? (and failure (not= failure (:failed (get links p))))]\n839:                 (assoc links p (cond-> link failure (assoc :failed failure)))\n840:                 (cond-> lines fresh? (conj (dial-line p source failure)))]))\n841:            [follower links []]\n862:         (assoc waiting principal {:trace trace :due (+ now delay)\n927:                              \") links it\"))))\n938:          [follower links dial-lines] (step-links follower node now)\n942:          links (reduce (fn [links {:keys [principal]}]\n943:                          (update links principal\n945:                        links\n959:                   (assoc ::follower follower)\n960:                   (update ::follow assoc :links links :waiting waiting))\n991:                        (assoc ::listen [host port])))\n997:                              [(assoc node ::publisher pub) ls])\n1006:              (assoc\n1014:              (assoc ::refusal (dht/refusal node)))\n1015:       shell (assoc shell :dht node)]\n1071:      (conj (str \"dht: solo, no --dht-peer, so no socket is opened; \"\n1076:      (conj (str \"dht: binding \" (address-text bind-host bind-port)\n1081:      (conj (str \"dht: publishing is ON. Everything in \" content\n1088:      (conj (str \"dht: publishing is on, but solo: nothing in \" content\n1092:      (conj (str\n1097:      (conj (str \"dht: --dht-manifest pins this run: following is suspended \"\n1101:      (conj (str \"dht: a (require ...) of a module this node does not hold \"\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-06 16:03:31 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 8b4bda87-5e50-47a0-b0c9-391dba6d3ca7\n\nThe tree compiles on Dart again, and all four items are fixed. Fixing item 1 also exposed a second Dart-only bug in the dial code. One change does reach the Architect's \"comes back to me\" cases: the cleanup in `open` was restructured (item 3), so the Architect should re-read `open`. The read-then-bind order, the reader's strictness and the shape of `compose` are unchanged.\n\n## 1. Dart compile failure (blocker)\n**Actual cause:** not the `.-length` warning, which was only a warning. I compiled `yin.repl.dht` alone with `clj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile yin.repl.dht`, and the compiler named the error:\n- `Not an expected argument name: .allowMalformed, valid names: ._allowMalformed`\n- Faulty form: `(convert/Utf8Decoder. .allowMalformed false)`, in the Dart branch of `decode-utf8`.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `decode-utf8` now uses `(.decode convert/utf8 ^Uint8List bs)`. Dart's default `utf8` codec already refuses malformed input with a `FormatException`, so decoding stays strict.\n- `byte-length` gets a `^Uint8List` type hint, which removes the dynamic warning.\n- `dht.cljc` now imports `Uint8List` the same way `sign.cljc` does.\n- `read-bounded` and `decode-utf8` stay in `dht.cljc`, so design 5.10 needs no change.\n\n**A second Dart-only bug, found by the focused run:** once the namespace compiled, 6 tests in `dht-head-test` failed on Dart because no dial was ever composed.\n- **Evidence:** the follower's `::follow :links` value printed as a *list* of link maps rather than a map. Each step-link had started from `nil` and done a multi-key `assoc` onto it.\n- **Fix:** each principal's link now starts as `{}` (`(get links p {})`).\n- I did not isolate the exact ClojureDart mechanism, only that starting from `{}` fixes it. The same tests pass on the JVM either way.\n\n## 2. A named pipe at `heads.edn` blocked startup\n- **Reproduced:** with the regular-file check disabled, the new FIFO test hit its deadline (\"the read did not block on the FIFO\" failed).\n- **Fix:** `read-bounded` refuses anything that is not a regular file, before any open that could block, with the message \"it is not a regular file\".\n  - A directory, FIFO or device is refused.\n  - A symlink is followed only when its target is a regular file; a dangling symlink is refused rather than read as absence.\n  - Node also opens with `O_NONBLOCK` and re-checks the opened descriptor with `fstat`.\n  - JVM and Dart check the type before opening; neither re-checks after open, so a swap between check and open is not covered there.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `heads-edn-must-be-a-regular-file` (portable): a directory, a symlink that is followed, and a dangling symlink.\n  - `a-fifo-at-heads-edn-is-refused-not-waited-on`: JVM-only and `^:slow`. It runs `mkfifo`, then reads in a child JVM with a 240 s deadline.\n  - No Node or Dart FIFO test.\n\n## 3. A failed cleanup masked the original refusal\n- **Reproduced:** with cleanup failures allowed to propagate, every case in the new test got a raw `IOException(\"close failed\")` with no `ex-data` instead of the refusal.\n- **Fix, and the reason the Architect should re-read `open`:** before the join, `open` closes only the directory store. Once joined, it closes only through the node, whose close shuts the socket and then (in a `finally`) the store. Both cleanups go through a new `quietly!`, so a failing close can never replace the original refusal.\n- **New seam:** `open` gains an `:open-store` option (the durable directory open), used by tests to make the store's close throw.\n- **Test:** `a-failed-cleanup-never-masks-the-refusal`. It covers a throwing socket close, a throwing store close, both, and a pre-join refusal with a throwing store close. Each case asserts:\n  - the original refusal (with `ex-data`) is what's thrown;\n  - binds equal socket closes, and the store is closed exactly once;\n  - the directory opens again afterwards.\n- **What the revert check doesn't cover:** it only proves the masking. The old double store close isn't re-created by that revert; the exactly-once assertion pins it against the new code only.\n\n## 4. Message on an unreadable `heads.edn`\nBoth messages now state the cost:\n- The unreadable-file refusal: \"move it aside to follow every principal from no head, dropping each one's rollback floor until a head is installed\".\n- The per-record refusal now ends \"…until a head is installed\".\n\n`yin.repl.md` already states this cost from round 2, so I left it unchanged.\n\n## Commands and outcomes\n- `clj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile yin.repl.dht`: before the fix, failed with the error above; after it, \"Compilation succeeded\".\n- `bb build:yin-repl-peer`: succeeded on the final tree; `build/yin-repl-peer` was generated.\n- `bb build:yin-repl-node`: build completed, 0 warnings.\n- Focused Dart runs via `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only …`:\n  - `yin.repl.dht-head-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`, `yin.repl.state-test`: **60 tests, all passed.**\n  - `yin.repl.dht-test`, `yin.repl.query-test`, `yin.repl.require-test`, `yin.repl.store-test`: **117 tests, all passed.**\n  - I ran this second set because `link.cljc`, `query.cljc` and `repl.cljc` changed in earlier rounds and the Dart lane never got past the build.\n- The 13-namespace JVM run: **268 tests, 2,837 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.**\n- `clj -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`: **3 tests, 131 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.**\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint` on `dht.cljc` and `dht_head_test.cljc`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- No Node test lane was run.\n\n**Touched this round:** `src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc` and `test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc`. No new files, nothing under `docs/design`, no git.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
